		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=20646#p20646"><![CDATA[
Would it be possible to separate the Physics API, Serialization and Authoring into sub sections of the forum? I don't really care at all about games using bullet or anything else other than the Maya Dynamica plugin, since this is what I use at work, and I work in Film / Television. Would be nice to have sections devoted to each topic instead of having to sift through tons of unrelated topics.<br><br>Next, is there any expectation when Bullet 3.0 will be ready? Things I would REALLY love to see implemented in the Maya plugin:<br><br>1) Breakable constraints! (yes I know this is *somewhat* possible to do already in Maya, but you have to use MEL which is slow, especially when you are iterating through 20k objects in your scene) This really should be a built in feature and running from compiled code so its fast.<br><br>2) Sleep / Force to Sleep of rigid bodies.<br><br>3) Any way to query through MEL, per frame, the rigidbodies that are in contact of each other, their velocity, and their contact points.<br><br>There's a bunch of other stuff I would like to see implemented, but if those 3 could somehow make it in the next release I think I might cry out of shear happiness, or at least make a donation somehow.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=7230">Fishypants</a> — Wed Oct 27, 2010 5:28 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
